\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Non-anticipating policy}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{agent}
\tag{policy}

\p{A \strong{non-anticipating policy} is a family of probability kernels}

##{
  \pi_t(da\mid H_t), \qquad t=0,1,\ldots,
}

\p{from public histories to actions. At time #{t}, the next action may depend
on #{H_t} and fresh policy randomness. It may not depend on a later
observation, a hidden state not encoded in #{H_t}, or the evaluator's future
decision.}

\p{This is the history-policy semantics of partially observable control,
specialized from \citef{kaelbling1998planning}. A language model implements
such a policy only after a decoder and an action-serialization rule have been
fixed. The model's next-token law alone does not determine a tool-level policy.}
